title: Codex app-server launch emits nonstandard alias and ambiguous log label
updated_at: "2026-07-12T08:23:24Z"
---
Problem

Starting a Codex session with `c2c new codex` currently emits a line like:

`[codex app-server] online-attached: alias=pihla-round endpoint=ws://127.0.0.1:37305`

The generated alias does not follow the normal managed Codex alias shape, and the log fields/label do not make c2c ownership explicit enough.

Acceptance criteria

1. An alias autogenerated for `c2c new codex` starts with `codex-` and ends with a random hexadecimal suffix, consistent with the normal autogenerated-alias convention. Explicit user-provided aliases remain unchanged.
2. The online-attached log field is named `c2c-alias=` instead of `alias=`.
3. The colored bracketed log prefix explicitly mentions c2c while retaining the useful Codex app-server context.
4. Focused regression tests cover the autogenerated alias shape and exact log labels/field names.

Blockers

None known. Preserve resume/restart identity semantics when changing autogenerated aliases.